1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,320
JC-PINN: a physics-informed model for additively manufactured AlSi10Mg.

2
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:15,892
The professor supplied 73 simulated stress–strain curves.

3
00:00:16,092 --> 00:00:22,563
Three temperatures, three strain rates, three densities, three shear moduli.

4
00:00:22,763 --> 00:00:27,679
Every curve softens, and its shape changes with temperature and rate.

5
00:00:27,879 --> 00:00:33,863
36 curves train the model; 37 are kept back for the final test.

6
00:00:35,563 --> 00:00:39,489
The governing law is our customised Johnson–Cook equation.

7
00:00:39,689 --> 00:00:45,956
Strain, rate, temperature, shear-modulus and porosity terms are multiplied.

8
00:00:46,156 --> 00:00:50,671
Fitted on its own, it misses the curves by about 10 %.

9
00:00:50,871 --> 00:00:55,759
A product of separate terms gives every condition the same curve shape.

10
00:00:57,459 --> 00:01:04,312
So the equation becomes the backbone, multiplied by a learned correction e^δ.

11
00:01:04,512 --> 00:01:10,184
Before training δ = 0, so the model starts as exactly the equation.

12
00:01:11,884 --> 00:01:16,721
Inside the network, the five inputs are first standardised.

13
00:01:16,921 --> 00:01:20,608
They pass through two hidden layers of 16 units each.

14
00:01:20,808 --> 00:01:28,063
Each unit adds its weighted inputs and a bias, then squashes the sum with tanh.

15
00:01:28,263 --> 00:01:34,456
Thicker wires carry stronger signals: blue pushes up, amber pushes down.

16
00:01:34,656 --> 00:01:39,494
The single output δ sets the correction factor at every strain.

17
00:01:41,194 --> 00:01:44,277
Training starts from the equation alone.

18
00:01:44,477 --> 00:01:50,883
1,500 Adam steps learn the curve shapes; L-BFGS then refines them.

19
00:01:51,083 --> 00:01:56,530
Mean training error falls from 8.95 to 0.35 MPa.

20
00:01:58,230 --> 00:02:04,439
14 settings, including physics penalties, were scored on training cases only.

21
00:02:04,639 --> 00:02:10,660
Cross-validation folds, plus whole temperature/rate groups hidden.

22
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:14,858
The best setting was locked before any test file was read.

23
00:02:16,558 --> 00:02:18,936
Five trained copies are averaged into one prediction.

24
00:02:19,136 --> 00:02:27,456
Test error: 0.44 MPa on 37 unseen cases, 17× better than the equation alone.

25
00:02:27,656 --> 00:02:31,507
The same network without the equation does slightly better (0.34 MPa).

26
00:02:31,707 --> 00:02:36,559
So the equation adds named physical constants, not accuracy.

27
00:02:38,259 --> 00:02:45,272
Valid for 30–200 °C at the simulated rates and porosities.

28
00:02:45,472 --> 00:02:50,720
Above 200 °C there is no data, so predictions there are unverified.
